<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="sec-section-TransformationsARC" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Effect of transformations on the average rate of change</title>

  <p> Now we formalize the observed relations between the average rate of change of a function <m>f</m> and the average rate of change of each of its respective transformations. </p>

  <p>
    <proposition xml:id="prop-ARCVerticalShift">
      <statement>
        <p>
          If <m>g(x)=f(x)+k</m>, then <md>
            ARC_{[a,b]}(g)=ARC_{[a,b]}(f)
          </md>
          
        </p>
      </statement>
    </proposition>
  </p>

  <p>
    <proof>
      <p>
        Since <m>g</m> is a vertical transformation of <m>f</m>, the <m>x-</m>values are not affected by the transformation. So, we compute the average rate of change of <m>g</m> over the same interval we compute the average rate of change of <m>f</m>. We have 
        <md>
            <mrow>ARC_{[a,b]}(g)= \amp\frac{g(b)-g(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> =\amp\frac{(f(b)+k)-(f(a)+k)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a} </mrow>
            <mrow> = \amp ARC_{[a,b]}(f) </mrow>
        </md>
        
        </p>
    </proof>
  </p>

  

</section>